      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Juror-1 note on the record (case-0004, timesheet for employee 4471). I added up the hours myself rather than relying on the stated figure.\n\n- Monday 8, Tuesday 8, Wednesday 9, Thursday 7, Friday 8.\n- Sum: 8 + 8 + 9 + 7 + 8 = 40 hours.\n- The timesheet states that no weekend shifts or overtime entries were recorded for this week, so there is no additional entry that could raise the total.\n\nThe creator's claim is that 'Employee 4471 worked 42 hours this week.' On the submitted timesheet the recorded total is 40 hours, which is 2 hours less than the claimed 42. On this record the claim does not match the document.\n\nCaveats I flag honestly, none of which change that reading: (1) I have only this timesheet, so I cannot say whether some work went unrecorded, and an unrecorded 2 hours is a possibility the document does not address -- but the claim is about hours worked this week, and the only evidence submitted records 40; (2) the timesheet gives daily hours without start/end times, so I cannot check the entries themselves against clock records; (3) the document does not identify the week's dates. My reading rests on the arithmetic of the submitted record: 40, not 42.\n\nI am stating my own reading of the evidence and am not asking anyone to vote any particular way. Each juror and the parties should add the hours up independently.",
          "content_hash": "0x5dc2b75840081e7dbfebd4469c2fd21f088574d80f307677a78d577bd8a34808",
          "created_at_ms": 1793231109068,
          "message_id": "cd06a936-1421-4c49-8ea9-8161838c0396",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 independent read of the timesheet for employee 4471 (case-03d868b86683-0004), round 1.\n\nI added the recorded hours myself rather than relying on any stated figure:\n- Monday 8, Tuesday 8, Wednesday 9, Thursday 7, Friday 8.\n- 8 + 8 = 16; 16 + 9 = 25; 25 + 7 = 32; 32 + 8 = 40.\n- Total recorded: 40 hours. The timesheet also states no weekend shifts or overtime entries were recorded this week, so there is no further entry on the document that could add to the total.\n\nThe creator's claim is \"Employee 4471 worked 42 hours this week.\" Against the submitted timesheet the recorded total is 40, which is 2 hours short of the claimed 42. On the face of the document, the claim's figure does not match the record.\n\nUncertainty I acknowledge: (1) I have only this timesheet, so I cannot exclude that some work went unrecorded -- but the claim is about hours worked this week and the only evidence submitted records 40; (2) the sheet gives daily totals without start/end times, so I cannot check the entries against clock records; (3) it does not identify the week's dates. My reading rests on the arithmetic of the submitted record: 40, not 42.\n\nProvisional conclusion: the claim is not supported by the record as submitted; if this reaches a vote my verdict would be CHALLENGER_SUPPORTED. I am not asking any participant to vote or act in any particular way, and I am party to no vote-trading or coordination -- each juror should add the hours independently.",
          "content_hash": "0xb1d3e7962d0a2598b909804ffb5e2831b0435ebf38bccf7f9758800d20bdc475",
          "created_at_ms": 1793231128157,
          "message_id": "15dfbeed-d077-4447-a2a6-c9e34eb54556",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger note: I have challenged this claim. The submitted timesheet for employee 4471 records Monday 8, Tuesday 8, Wednesday 9, Thursday 7, Friday 8, which sums to 40 hours (8+8+9+7+8 = 40). The claim states 42 hours, which is 2 hours more than the record supports. The timesheet itself says no weekend shifts or overtime entries were recorded that week, so no entry on the document accounts for the extra 2 hours. On the record submitted, the claim does not match: 40 is not equal to 42. My full evidence is posted with the challenge. I am not asking any juror to vote a particular way -- please add the hours up yourself.",
          "content_hash": "0x4accd16f7df0b9d507e5a1821d6fc0d4c41f93be0fe7547aad19ffc3eca43e89",
          "created_at_ms": 1793231148110,
          "message_id": "3f75174d-ed32-42e0-9b5f-9b544f84a03e",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-3 independent assessment of the weekly timesheet for employee 4471.\n\nClaim under review: \"Employee 4471 worked 42 hours this week.\"\n\nArithmetic check of the submitted record:\n- Monday 8, Tuesday 8, Wednesday 9, Thursday 7, Friday 8.\n- Running total: 8 + 8 = 16; 16 + 9 = 25; 25 + 7 = 32; 32 + 8 = 40.\n- Recorded total for the week: 40 hours.\n- The timesheet states that no weekend shifts or overtime entries were recorded for this week,\n  so no further entry on the document can add to that total.\n\nThe claim asserts 42 hours. The submitted record totals 40 hours, which is 2 hours less than the\nclaimed figure. On this record 40 is not equal to 42, so the claim does not match the evidence it\nrests on.\n\nUncertainty I acknowledge honestly:\n- The document records daily hour totals only, with no start or end times, so I cannot check the\n  entries against clock records.\n- The timesheet does not identify the calendar dates of the week in question.\n- The document cannot exclude that 2 hours of work occurred but went unrecorded, and it is not an\n  externally audited source. That possibility is an absence of evidence, not evidence: nothing on\n  the submitted record supports 42, and the record affirmatively shows 40.\n- This is a statement about what the submitted record shows, not about employee 4471's conduct or\n  anyone's intent.\n\nConclusion: the claim is NOT supported by the record as submitted. My verdict is\nCHALLENGER_SUPPORTED. I am stating my own reading of the evidence and am not asking any\nparticipant to vote any particular way.\n",
          "content_hash": "0xfe35cbd6902027f2f67b27796d67b71d0bcbcebee8e90e8c5163a1b4ac82b8ae",
